# Execution engine structure

## Types

Shared types live in `src/types/` (`protocol.ts` = website siblings; other files match MCP catalog / lab / verbs). Import from `../types/index.js` (barrel). Do not add a root `src/types.ts`.

## Generic library vs catalog

- **Query shapes** (`simulate`, `transaction`, `block`, `probe`, later `generate`) are the stable API — not per-EIP or per-fork functions
- **Named forks** (`namedForks` in `describeCapabilities()`) are first-class capabilities: summary, keywords, shapes, advertised `relatedEips`. Callers can run under Glamsterdam / Fusaka / Pectra without naming an EIP
- **EIP modules** (`src/modules/eip-NNNN/`) describe what became possible: `summary`, `opcodes`, encoding, `keywords`, `runnable`
- Only `runnable: true` modules belong in `EIP_MODULES` / `describeCapabilities().eips`

## Catalog honesty

- Unimplemented or website-only EIPs stay **off** the live catalog
- Modules describe **support**, not pedagogical demo programs
- Demo bytecode belongs in `src/__tests__/fixtures/`, not module descriptors

## Service boundaries (do not break)

- Isolated lab / BYOS — no archive node, no mainnet or L2 RPC. Callers supply bytecode, txs, **and constructed prestate** (accounts, code, storage). Empty world is not required.
- `run_bytecode` / `simulateBytecode` is a **VM message-call** (`createVM` + `runCall`) with `gasUsedScope: call-frame`. Do not use detached `runCode` (SSTORE cannot persist that path).
- Call isolation is the default — each engine call is a pure function of its input. Do not hide EVM in process globals. Optional snapshot continuation belongs in the gateway later, not as implicit engine state.
- Raw bytecode only — no Solidity compile in the engine
- Provenance on every simulate result
- No sequential multi-block **historical** backtesting (a lab `run_block` of constructed txs is in scope)

## Gateway boundary

This repo has **no MCP transport**. Tool names and Zod schemas live in `mcp-gateway`. Engine exports library functions and types only.

## When editing

- Register new modules in `src/modules/index.ts`
- Run `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test:ci`, `npm run lf:ci` before finishing
- Human EIP pages live in `website/mcp-docs/use/eips/` — link, do not duplicate long prose in code
